-- issue #1383, verbatim from the issue body.
-- Hand-derived correct answer: `100`. `mkH : Holder`; `Holder`'s sole variant
-- is the named-field constructor `Plain { hx : Int }`; `mkH.hx` projects `hx`
-- from it. `plainlib`'s `Plain` is a different declaration in a different
-- namespace position (a record TYPE, not this constructor) and is irrelevant
-- to this projection.
import ahold.{Holder, mkH}
import plainlib.{Plain, mkP}
main : <IO> Unit
main = putStrLn (intToString mkH.hx)
